{
  "intro": "One room, twelve men, and a commission with no geographic ceiling: witnesses in Jerusalem, in all Judea and Samaria, and to the uttermost parts of the earth. This map draws what the record can actually support — real coastlines, cities at true coordinates, each road running from Jerusalem along its claimed corridor to the place where the man's trail ends. The line itself tells you how much to trust it: solid where scripture speaks, dashed where an early source speaks, dotted where only later tradition does. Three seats get no road at all — two the record cannot honestly place, and one that was never sent; they are listed beneath the map. And the ring at the center is the seat scripture itself keeps in Jerusalem. That restraint is the point of this site.",
